# LINE ENDINGS FOR THE CONTRACT FILES.
#
# core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes means git stores LF and checks out CRLF, so the
# worktree bytes and the blob bytes of the same file at the same commit differ -- and a hash over
# one disagrees with a hash over the other with nothing visibly wrong. That is the failure that
# broke golden #5's fnv1a check.
#
# TAPE-SCHEMA.tsv is the human-readable half of the record format: the file check_schema.py
# cross-checks against evctape_schema.json, and the one an analyst reads to learn what a column
# means. It was rewritten with CRLF by accident this session (a Python text-mode write) and had to
# be normalised back by hand -- exactly the class of silent byte change this pin prevents.
#
# Matches the pin on the machine schema in D:/mandalark-cascade-research/.gitattributes, so the
# two halves of one contract cannot drift in encoding either.
#
# Deliberately narrow: the file whose bytes are a contract, not the whole tree.
harness/TAPE-SCHEMA.tsv   text eol=lf
